<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36179" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔντεα</span></b> , τά, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fighting gear, arms, armour,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ. ἀρήϊα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					10.407
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				23.368
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ. πατρός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					19.17
				</span></i>
			; esp. <i>coat of mail, corslet,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				10.34
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔντε᾽ ἔδυνεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					3.339
				</span></i>
			, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>furniture, appliances, tackle,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ. δαιτός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					7.232
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ. νηός</span>”
				<i>rigging,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					h.Ap.
					489
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				4.70
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ. ἵππεια</span>
			<i>trappings, harness,</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				9.22
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>P.</u>
				4.235
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔντη δίφρου</span>”
				<i>harness,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					194
				</span></i>
			 (but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔντεα</span> alone for
				<i>chariots,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				4.24
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔντεα αὐλῶν</span> periphr.
			for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐλοί,</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				7.12
			</span></i>; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔντεα</span> alone,
				<i>musical instruments,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>P.</u>
				12.21
			</span></i>; of the <i>instruments</i> of the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Γάλλαι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Lyr.Adesp.</u>
				121
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔντεα Φοίβου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Ap.</u>
					19
				</span></i>
			.—
				Ep.
			 and Lyr. word, once in Trag. (v. supr.):—sg.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔντος</span> only in <i><span class="en">
				Archil.
				6
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
